## Actions

1. (25) Promises sweep: any "deferred to post-conference analysis"
   (pre-chain site L2014 — 0582 may have removed it; re-grep), "We
   defer more observations with more models" (not found verbatim at
   planning time — search "defer", "future work will", "will be
   reported", "companion" variants). Promises are deleted, not
   hedged.
2. (38) Noise phrases, author's list: "now scored for all runs"
   (L781), "minimum attainable p…" (L786), "bear evidence" (variants —
   not found verbatim), "we don't do statistical tests" (variants).
   Delete or fold into substantive sentences.
3. (26, 17-class) Register sweep: lab-journal narration ("we then
   ran…", session/ops chronology, harness details in prose) →
   technical-report register; overcomplicated passages → plain
   authorial tone (model: the §7.1 rewrite from ticket 0585).
4. (13-class) Instruction-cruft sweep: generation/layout instructions
   surviving as prose (model: "names read left-to-right, no
   rotation").
5. (33-class) AI-English doublet sweep: adverb+adverb /
   intensifier-pair patterns ("solidly and firmly" class).

## Test

- Negative guards for the literal noise phrases above (those still
  present at execution time) — red now, green after. Class-level
  regex guards where a lexically stable signature exists (CI polarity
  rule: forbid what must not be said; never pin new positive
  phrasings).

